# Top-level runtime dependencies of the embeddings service IMAGE
# (python/Dockerfile). The installed lock is requirements-service.txt,
# GENERATED from this file with hashes (F9-6) — never edit the lock by hand:
#
#   docker run --rm --platform linux/arm64 -v "$PWD/python:/w" -w /w \
#     python:3.13.15-slim-bookworm@sha256:2325bb286ec344af3e5898cc224b5844e2707ac6e26b1632516fd3edc84a5e26 \
#     sh -c "pip install pip-tools && pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --strip-extras \
#            --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu \
#            --output-file requirements-service.txt requirements-service.in"
#
# (pip-tools records the hashes of EVERY file of each pinned version, so one
# run covers the x86_64 and aarch64 images.) Separate from requirements.txt,
# which carries the dev/test toolchain and runs on CI's Python 3.11.
#
# torch: the CPU-only build from the PyTorch index — the default PyPI wheel
# pulls ~2 GB of CUDA libraries this CPU service never loads.
